Z||000000||Monkeyman||12-11-1999||04:00 AM||||There are a couple of us interested in custom dashes.  I was sent this site address.  Pretty cool dash.  Maybe Cliff knows who it is.  The dash builder is from the Netherlands, too, I think.  <A HREF="http://members.tripod.lycos.nl/FIERO_2/thumbnails-1.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.tripod.lycos.nl/FIERO_2/thumbnails-1.html</A>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cool_dash-door_3.jpg">      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cool_dash-6_2.jpg">   <P><BR>[This message has been edited by Monkeyman (edited 12-11-1999).]<p>[This message has been edited by Monkeyman (edited 12-11-1999).]||||reg||7
Z||000001||RZURCTN||12-11-1999||10:25 AM||||That's a pretty cool looking setup!  I wish I knew how to fabricate stuff like that!  Is there a "Do IT Yourself Kit" for building your 'custom dash'?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Shiner||12-11-1999||10:34 AM||||A great guy by the name of Eddy Snaauw made this dash.  He took an original dash, and started building onto it and cutting it apart.  He finished it, and made a mold.  I personally think it's the most beautiful dash ever made for a fiero.  You would be able to do it anyway you want to also, if you wanted it covered in leather, painted, whatever.  He told me he is currently talking to a few distributors in the US, with plans to sell them the molds.  I hope this one comes over the sea to us; it would be the nicest on the market!||||reg||1
Z||000003||william_thorniii||12-11-1999||03:52 PM||||Eddy is a great guy.  I am trying to help him out with his webpage.  I still think that his dash is the most attractive that I have ever seen.  Furthermore, I think that it will really make our Fiero's look MUCH more modern<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000004||Formula||12-11-1999||04:47 PM||||what do you need to make your own dash?||||reg||1
Z||000005||88GT||12-11-1999||05:02 PM||||That is a very nice dash.  I would love to put one of those in my 88GT (when I get it next year).  Anybody have an idea on proposed price?<P>James||||reg||1
Z||000006||DaRkLoRD||12-11-1999||05:22 PM||||To build a custom dash/console, you basically need: an idea of what you want it to look like, rigid foam insulation, wood frame (or the original dash if you're building on top of that), expanding foam, bondo, fiberglass, lots and lots of free time, leather or vinyl to cover it with, did I mention lots of free time? oh yeah. and plenty of time to work on it.<P>Take a look at this site, explains the process they went through while designing a new dash and console.  <A HREF="http://www.perigee.net/~lunapark/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.perigee.net/~lunapark/</A>  <P>Check out this how-to article on constructing things (in this case, a car body) out of foam insulation and fiberglass.<P> <A HREF="http://www.rqriley.com/frp-foam.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rqriley.com/frp-foam.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||12-11-1999||06:37 PM||||I just talked to Eddy myself.  He said that he hopes it will be marketed by spring of 2000.  Does everybody know about Eddy and his dash?  I thought I was giving everyone some new info.  Guess not. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Darklord--You forgot to mention that you also need LOTS and LOTS and LOTS and LOTS and LOTS and LOTS of patience.  I'm building my own dash and I never knew how frustrating it could be.  Mine doesn't look nearly as good as his, though.  Maybe, when I get it done, I'll post some pics of it.  Then again, after seeing Eddys' dash, I may be too embarrassed. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||DaRkLoRD||12-11-1999||07:27 PM||||I didn't know about the dash until I found it last night and sent it to you.. it's a very cool dash.. a bit round compared to the exterior lines of the Fiero however. But very nice. One of the best I've seen actually.<P>I've been talking with Monkeyman over email for a while now, and I have some pretty good ideas on making a custom dash. I might put a section on my website (Fiero Project) about this, with links to other similar projects, how-to articles, as well as lots and lots of pictures.||||reg||1
Z||000009||william_thorniii||12-11-1999||09:11 PM||||Dark,<P>While I agree with you that it is more rounded than the exterior of the Fiero... I wouldn't say that it is too rounded.  I think it is reminiscent of a Nissan 300ZX of the mid 90's.  I think that it along with a few (minor) body mods could make a Fiero look slightly more modern... maybe like some of the fabled 1989 protos that some say are still around.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||14
Z||000010||DaRkLoRD||12-11-1999||09:19 PM||||Everything depends on opinion I guess! but you're right, with a few mods the Fiero could look quite modern. not that it doesn't already look it, there are a few things that could make it look like a late 90s car. one of which is more curved surfaces, new tail lights.. maybe a new front end. (exactly the mods I want to do in fact!)<P>I have photos of the 1989 Fiero prototype, it's awesome. wish someone would make a kit based on the 89 or 90 prototype.||||reg||1
